  "english": "Eve of the Fast of the Nativity.\n30. Tuesday. Tone 8 [Dk]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Fathers [Harts] of the Fast: Tone 8 [Dk], \"Blessed art Thou, Lord God of our fathers\" (Orhneal ter astuats hartsn). And the rest according to order.\n\nJanuary\n4. Sunday. Tone 4 [Bk]. Seventh Sunday of the Fast. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi]: Tone 3 [Bk], \"They anticipated\" (Kankhetsin), to the end.\n5. Monday. Tone 5 [Gd]. Eve [Chragaluyts] of the Nativity of Christ.\n3. [Psalm verses] \"The divine\" (Zastuatsayin), and \"Thy resurrection\" (Zko yarutiund), and \"Taking also our\" (Areal ev mer).\n22. Monday. Tone 7 [Dz]. Abraham and Khoren, Cosmas and Damian, and the martyr Adeodatus [Astuatsatur]. Fathers [Harts]: Tone 4 [Bk], \"Who in the battle\" (Ork i marti).\n23. Tuesday. Tone 8 [Dk]. David the Prophet, and James the Apostle.\n28. Sunday. Tone 5 [Gd]. Sixth Sunday. Fathers [Harts]: Tone 6 [Gk], \"Pre-eternal\" (Nakhahavitean). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi]: Tone 5 [Gd], \"Glorified is Thy\" (Paravoreal e ko), to the end.\n29. Monday. Tone 6 [Gk]. Sons of Thunder [Vorotman].\n\nThe Roman Seven-Day Cycle 2.\n26. Saturday. Tone 5 [Gd]. Fathers Athanasius and Cyril.\n27. Sunday. Tone 6 [Gk]. Second Sunday. Fathers [Harts]: Tone 5 [Gd], \"Creator of all creatures\" (Ararichd araratsots). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi]: Tone 6 [Gk], \"The vision like lightning\" (Tesil paylaknadzev).\n28. Monday. Tone 7 [Dz]. Eugenius, Macarius, and the others. Fathers [Harts]: Tone 3 [Gd], \"Who dost not bear grudges\" (Anokhakal).\n29. Tuesday. Tone 8 [Dk]. The holy general Andrew and his army, and the others.\n31. Thursday. Tone 2 [Ak]. Adrian and his wife Anatolia, and the others. Fathers [Harts]: Tone 3 [Gd], \"With Thy saints\" (End surbs ko).\n\nFebruary\n2. Saturday. Tone 4 [Bk]. Gregory the Theologian.\n3. Sunday. Tone 5 [Gd]. Third Sunday. Fathers [Harts]: Tone 6 [Gk], \"Today the unslain\" (Aysor zzenav). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi]: Tone 5 [Gd], \"Glorified [is Thy]\" (Paravoreal).\n4. Monday. Tone 6 [Gk]. The Maccabees, Eleazar, and the others. Fathers [Harts]: Tone 4 [Bk], \"We bless Thee, Lord\" (Orhnemk zkhez ter).\n5. Tuesday. Tone 7 [Dz]. The twelve prophets: Hosea, and the others.\n\nJanuary\n6. SUNDAY. Tone 1 [Adz]. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The period between this and Great Lent is thirty-six days.\n14. Monday. Tone 1 [Adz]. John the Forerunner [Karapet].\n15. Tuesday. Tone 2 [Ak]. Bishop Peter, Blaise, and the others.\n16. Wednesday. Tone 3 [Bd]. Fathers [Harts] of the Fast: Tone 3 [Bd], \"Who didst deliver\" (Or apregutser).\n17. Thursday. Tone 4 [Bk]. Anton the Hermit.\n19. Saturday. Tone 6 [Gk]. King Theodosius, and the Children of Ephesus.\n20. Sunday. Tone 7 [Dz]. First Sunday. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi]: Tone 5 [Gd], \"The resurrection of the Son of God\" (Zyarutiun astuatsordvoyn).\n21. Monday. Tone 8 [Dk]. Cyricus and Julitta, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris. Fathers [Harts]: Tone 2 [Ak], \"Holy God Creator\" (Surb astuats ararich).\n22. Tuesday. Tone 1 [Adz]. Vahan of Goghtn, and Eugenia the virgin, and the others. Fathers [Harts]: Tone 2 [Ak], \"Who art Most High\" (Or bardzreald es).\n24. Thursday. Tone 3 [Bd]. Tryphon, Barsamas, and Onuphrius the hermits.",
